<%- /*
Scaffolded by jvm-service (internal/flavor/definitions.go), which detects pom.xml, build.gradle,
build.gradle.kts, mvnw or gradlew. Adoption makes the test job a required check, so the build step
runs whichever build the repository carries and names what is missing instead of failing on a
layout it did not model. A wrapper committed without its executable bit (Git records the mode, and
Windows checkouts often drop it) still runs through sh. TestJVMBuildStepRunsTheRepositorysBuild
(internal/flavor/jvm_ci_test.go) executes the step against each layout.

The trigger, the draft step and every later step's condition are the hosted gate shape
(templates/hostedgate.go, defined in internal/ghworkflow/hostedgate.go): the job runs on a push to
the default branch and on every pull request activity that can change what merges, and on a draft
it fails in its first step, saying it runs when the pull request is marked ready (#817). Every
rendering this body or an earlier one produced is recorded (internal/flavor/ci_prior.go), so an
unedited copy is refreshed without --force.
*/ -%>
---
name: CI

<% hostedGateOn %>
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-26.04
    steps:
<% hostedGateDraftStep %>
      - name: Checkout source<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Setup Java<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: '25'

      # jvm-service matches Maven and Gradle builds alike, so the step runs
      # whichever the repository carries, preferring a checked-in wrapper over
      # the runner's own install.
      - name: Build and verify<% hostedGateStepIf %>
        run: |
          if [ -x ./mvnw ]; then
            ./mvnw -B verify
          elif [ -f ./mvnw ]; then
            sh ./mvnw -B verify
          elif [ -f pom.xml ]; then
            mvn -B verify
          elif [ -x ./gradlew ]; then
            ./gradlew check
          elif [ -f ./gradlew ]; then
            sh ./gradlew check
          elif [ -f build.gradle ] || [ -f build.gradle.kts ] ||
            [ -f settings.gradle ] || [ -f settings.gradle.kts ]; then
            if command -v gradle >/dev/null 2>&1; then
              gradle check
            else
              echo "Gradle build has no gradlew wrapper and the runner" \
                "no gradle; commit one: gradle wrapper" >&2
              exit 1
            fi
          else
            echo "no Maven or Gradle build found" >&2
            exit 1
          fi
